{"body":"# A consent notification to an HIU bridge

## In plain words

When a patient decides on your consent request, ABDM posts the decision to your [HIU](/docs/hiecm/v3/getting-started/glossary#hiu) bridge at `/api/v3/hiu/consent/request/notify`. The path is relative to the callback URL you registered. Acknowledge each notification by calling [consent HIU on-notify](/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m3/endpoints/m3-consent-management-data-flow-hiu/03-m3-post-consent-v3-request-hiu-on-notify).

## Before you start

A callback URL registered for your bridge and reachable from the public internet.

## What happens

ABDM posts with the `REQUEST-ID`, `TIMESTAMP` and `X-HIU-ID` headers, and expects 200 OK. Then acknowledge on `/api/hiecm/consent/v3/request/hiu/on-notify`, with this notification's `REQUEST-ID` as `requestId`.

## When it goes wrong

No notification arrives: check that the callback URL is public, registered and quick to answer. Make the handler idempotent on `consentRequestId` and `status`.","catalogue_version":"2026.09.16","doc_url":"/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m3/endpoints/m3-callbacks/03-m3-post-v3-hiu-consent-request-notify#m2-on-consent-notify-hiu","gateway":"hiecm","id":"hiecm.callback.m2-on-consent-notify-hiu","milestone":"M2","operation":"m3_post_v3_hiu_consent_request_notify","summary":"ABDM posts a patient's consent decision to the HIU's bridge, which acknowledges it through hiu on-notify.","title":"A consent notification to an HIU bridge","type":"callback"}
